  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering App Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on determining the best architecture for this application. Given the \"Solo Leveling\" theme and high-performance requirement, I\'m leaning toward a React-based front-end with a Node.js or Python (Flask or FastAPI) back-end. I must decide whether to use server-side rendering or a static site to get the best performance. The design system and UI screenshots are guiding my component choices.\n\n\n**Adapting to Constraints**\n\nI\'ve hit a slight snag, or rather, a redirection. The user requested React Native and Expo, but our environment favors a React/Vite web application. I\'m now shifting my focus to crafting a web app that perfectly emulates the mobile experience. The goal is a highly polished, responsive web interface that mirrors the requested mobile screen designs. We\'ll leverage React, Vite, and Tailwind to achieve this.\n\n\n**Defining Interactive Screens**\n\nI am now visualizing the interactive components of each screen, ensuring the experience is dynamic and engaging. My focus is on making the \"Training Mode\" particularly immersive, integrating timers, audio cues, and clear visual feedback for the user. I\'m prioritizing seamless navigation between screens, animations, and transitions to maintain a polished feel throughout. I am confident that these features will increase the user\'s enjoyment.\n\n\n**Clarifying Feature Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the scope of interactive training mode and daily quest completion. I\'m focusing on \"Start Training\" integration with a functional dashboard, including the stopwatch and rep incrementation, and Quest Completed screen styling as a core feature. I need to make sure I am focusing on what is requested in the screenshots, and make sure that this is a *simple* app. I am reassessing navigation restrictions to ensure a direct, streamlined user flow.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Screen Fidelity**\n\nI am now squarely focused on achieving high fidelity in the requested screens (Training, Stats, Profile, Quest Details, and Quest Completed). The user\'s screen-specific requirements mandate active interactions and bottom navigation. I need to make sure to leverage React state for full functionality, but the available skills don\'t seem like a perfect fit, so it will be a fully client-side tracker. I\'m focusing on ensuring these screens function and flow together perfectly.\n\n\n**Analyzing Image Integration**\n\nI\'m now examining the image resources in the provided HTML. The user\'s links include anatomical silhouettes and profile images. I will determine how best to integrate these assets to maintain the desired aesthetic, using the HTML image links directly, rather than relying on generation. This will save a good amount of time, and retain visual consistency.\n\n\n**Integrating Profile Images**\n\nI am now focusing on integrating the provided profile images. I\'ve located several avatars within the HTML, including close-ups with distinctive glowing eyes. My plan is to incorporate these images directly, ensuring the visual style is consistent with the user\'s links. I will be directly linking these images for optimal visual integrity and to save time. I am confident that their look will be consistent.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will start by analyzing the current codebase to understand the existing setup, package definitions, and configuration files. This will allow me to integrate the hunter levelling system, combining the multi-screen system of the Solo Leveling HUD with interactive state, responsive mobile simulation containers, and immersive visual design. Let\'s inspect the files.   \n\nFirst, I\'ll view `package.json` to see if there are any additional libraries we might find useful or if are missing any icons. I\'ll also check `metadata.json` so I can update the app\'s name and description."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 882233949
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
