  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Layout Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into building layout components! My goal is to create separate components for each tab, to keep the code clean and manageable, and prevent a monstrous App.tsx. Right now, I\'m thinking about the structure of HunterOnboarding, which is a form.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Interface**\n\nI\'ve hit a wave of inspiration! Now I\'m focused on making the UI fully playable. \"Start Quest\" or \"Start Training\" should trigger an interactive workout interface with rep counters that increment level trackers. Completing a quest should trigger a \"QUEST COMPLETED\" overlay with animated stat increases! The potential for interactivity is massive!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create `/src/components/PhoneSimulator.tsx`. To give the user the precise look and feel of an actual React Native & Expo app running on their phone, this component wraps the entire experience in an incredibly polished phone simulator. It features a realistic speaker grill, battery indicators, cellular signal bars, Wi-Fi symbols, and a camera notch. On desktop, it renders as a sleek, physical smartphone centered on a dark canvas, while automatically scaling to full bleed on actual mobile browsers. Let\'s write the code."
