    thinking: "**Defining the UI for Hunter Profile**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the user interface for the Hunter Profile screen, specifically `/src/components/ProfileView.tsx`. I\'ve visualized the top header as \"ARISE\" with a hamburger menu and user avatar. Next, I am breaking down the contents, like the Profile ID Card using a sleek card layout.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Profile Card**\n\nI\'m currently visualizing the Hunter Profile ID card, specifically the layout for Jung Sinwoo. I am working on a visual design with a purple neon border, featuring an avatar photo and a large \"RANK S\" badge. I am planning the placement of the character name, handle, and grid-like parameters for Class, Title, Age and Level. I am also planning the placement of the level as \"LV. 99\" and incorporating a \"Level Progression\" indicator. Finally, I\'m integrating the ability score as a glass-panel styled box with purple neon borders.\n\n\n**Rendering the Radar Chart**\n\nI\'ve just rendered an interactive SVG radar chart with concentric pentagons and axis vectors, displaying Hunter stats. It features incrementing handlers that allow real-time polygon morphing. Below the chart, there are numeric stat columns, allowing users to increase their stats with a simple tap. It is a masterpiece! I\'m now implementing a \"Growth Progression\" section, which will use a bar chart to show training cycles.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create the fourth screen `/src/components/ProfileView.tsx` representing the **Hunter Stats Profile Room** shown in Screenshot 4. It includes an Obsidian Character ID Board displaying S-Rank rating status, fighter classifications, handle details (`@shadow_monarch_99`), and progress tracks for level increments (e.g. Lvl 99). It features an interactive **SVG Radar Chart** plotting five traits (Strength, Agility, Endurance, Recovery, and Discipline) that updates and morphs in real-time when stats are changed. It also builds weekly Growth Progression bar graphs and a 2x2 Achievements Matrix (Shadow Monarch, First Dungeon Cleared, Master of Shadows, 100 Day Grind). Let\'s write the code."
